.TH GARNER 1 "" "garner" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
garner \- internal deb and rpm package repository
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B garner
.I command
.RI [ arguments ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B garner
serves signed apt and dnf repositories from uploaded packages and from
releases synced from GitHub, GitLab and Forgejo/Gitea.
.PP
Local commands run on the host that holds the configuration and the
database.
API commands talk to a running server over HTTP and can run anywhere.
Flags may appear before or after positional arguments;
.B \-\-
ends flag parsing.
.SH LOCAL COMMANDS
.TP
.B serve \fR[\fB\-\-config \fIFILE\fR]
Run the server.
.B SIGHUP
reloads the configuration;
.B SIGTERM
and
.B SIGINT
stop it.
Under systemd it reports readiness through
.B \%NOTIFY_SOCKET
and accepts listening sockets passed with
.BR \%LISTEN_FDS .
.TP
.B init \fR[\fB\-\-config \fIFILE\fR]
Create the storage directory, the database, a signing key when
.B signing.keys
is empty, and an admin token.
The token is printed once.
Running it again keeps an existing key, and creates no token when any
token exists.
.TP
.BR "config validate" " [\fIFILE\fR]"
Check a configuration file and print its hash.
Works offline and does not open files that
.B *_file
keys point to.
.TP
.B token create \-\-name \fIN\fB \-\-owner \fIO\fB \-\-scope \fIS\fR[,\fIS\fR...]
.TQ
.B token list
.TQ
.B token revoke \fINAME\fR
Manage API tokens.
Scopes are
.BR upload ,
.B publish
and
.BR admin .
By default these open the database directly, which fails while
.B garner serve
runs; with
.B \-\-url
they go through the API and need an
.B admin
token.
.SH API COMMANDS
The server is taken from
.BR \-\-url ,
then
.BR GARNER_URL ,
then
.BR \%http://localhost:8080 .
Commands that change state need a token in
.B \%GARNER_TOKEN
with the scope listed.
Listing commands accept
.B \-\-json
to print the raw response.
.TP
.B upload \fR[\fB\-\-suite \fIS\fR] [\fB\-\-release \fIR\fR] \fIFILES\fR...
Upload .deb or .rpm files into a deb suite or rpm release.
Scope:
.BR upload .
.TP
.B remove \fINAME\fR \fR[\fB\-\-version \fIV\fR] [\fB\-\-arch \fIA\fR] [\fB\-\-distribution \fID\fR]
Remove the matching versions of a package.
Scope:
.BR admin .
.TP
.B owner list
.TQ
.B owner set \fINAME OWNER\fR
Show or change which owner may upload a package name.
.B set
needs scope
.BR admin .
.TP
.B sync \fISOURCE\fR
Start a sync of a configured source; follow it with
.BR "garner status" .
Scope:
.BR publish .
.TP
.B approve \fIPACKAGE_ID\fR
Release a held package.
Scope:
.BR publish .
.TP
.BR "conflicts list" " [" \-\-all ]
Show open conflicts, or all with
.BR \-\-all .
Scope:
.BR publish .
.TP
.B packages list \fR[\fB\-\-name \fIN\fR] [\fB\-\-distribution \fID\fR] [\fB\-\-all\fR]
List packages; removed ones only with
.BR \-\-all .
.TP
.B snapshot list
.TQ
.B snapshot rollback \fIID\fR
List published snapshots, or publish a new snapshot with the packages of
.IR ID .
.B rollback
needs scope
.BR publish .
.TP
.B publish
Publish a new snapshot.
Scope:
.BR publish .
.TP
.B gc
Delete package files and snapshots that are no longer referenced.
Scope:
.BR admin .
.TP
.B reload
Reload the server's configuration, like
.BR SIGHUP .
Scope:
.BR admin .
.TP
.B status
Show the version, configuration, current snapshot, open conflicts, held
packages and the state of each source.
.SH OTHER COMMANDS
.TP
.BR version ", " \-\-version
Print the version.
.TP
.BR help ", " \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a usage summary.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B GARNER_URL
Server URL for API commands and
.BR "token \-\-url" .
.TP
.B \%GARNER_TOKEN
API token as
.IB NAME : SECRET\fR,
as printed by
.B garner init
and
.BR "garner token create" .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/garner/garner.yaml
Default configuration file; see
.BR garner.yaml (5).
.TP
.I /var/lib/garner
Default storage directory and SQLite database.
.TP
.I /usr/share/doc/garner/design.md.gz
Design document.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
The command failed, or at least one file of an upload failed.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error.
.SH EXAMPLES
First start of a packaged install:
.PP
.RS
.nf
sudo -u garner garner init
systemctl enable \-\-now garner
.fi
.RE
.PP
Upload a package from CI:
.PP
.RS
.nf
export GARNER_URL=https://pkg.example.com
export GARNER_TOKEN=ci:...
garner upload \-\-suite stable dist/*.deb
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR garner.yaml (5),
.BR apt (8),
.BR dnf (8),
.BR systemctl (1)
